From 168e9b986e29e7f2cc0b24ec14bc16e39d3452cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sri Adarsh Kumar <sri.adarsh.kumar+gh@zalando.de>
Date: Sun, 8 Feb 2026 13:41:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] Add JsonParser.readText(Writer) for truly non-buffering
 string reads

Implements #1288 (originally #15) to support streaming large JSON string
values without buffering entire content in memory.

Key changes:
- Add abstract readText(Writer) method to JsonParser with documentation
  explaining consumption semantics
- Implement _streamString(Writer) in UTF8StreamJsonParser,
  ReaderBasedJsonParser, and UTF8DataInputJsonParser that read and decode
  content byte-by-byte/char-by-char and write directly to Writer
- Handle UTF-8 multi-byte sequences, escape sequences, and surrogate pairs
  during streaming
- Content is consumed after read (TextBuffer cleared), making string
  unavailable for subsequent getString() calls
- Update getString(Writer) javadocs to clarify buffering behavior
- NonBlockingJsonParserBase falls back to getString(Writer) as streaming
  not applicable for async parsing
- Add test coverage verifying consumption behavior and correctness

Unlike getText(Writer), this method bypasses TextBuffer entirely and
StreamReadConstraints validation, enabling processing of strings larger
than maxStringLength limit without memory issues.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
